{
 "comment": "clause44: a plain round-off line (a round-off ledger with no role of its own) is shown exactly where the line it rounds is shown: the voucher's first expenditure line that is read by the party, else its first other expenditure line, else non-supply. On a journal with no party or one whose party is an expense or income ledger it takes that reason, a debit or a credit; beside bank charges or bank interest (forced) it is forced with them and counted as forced; beside a partner's remuneration, a mixed ledger, a depreciation line or a no-supplier line it takes that reason; round-off first, then bank charges, then bank interest follows the charges; a line read by the party wins over an earlier forced one, a credit one too; on a capital invoice whose only other lines are not expenditure (a zero purchase line is no row) it is non-supply; two round-off lines both follow; beside an own-role round-off ledger it follows that line; and a round-off ledger given its own category, depreciation or no-supplier role is placed by that role whatever it rounds. Every GSTIN is invented (fourteenth character Y).",
